@meteorcloudy we still have `--watchfs` disabled for Angular, presumably this is hurting us for Mac/Linux rebuild performance. ( https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/29541 referenced above)

I'm now creating a .bazelrc file to share with all frontend projects. I would rather not copy this setting for everyone, but we do need things to work on Windows out of the box.

A shorter term solution would be if the .bazelrc setting could be platform-dependent, similar to how the --config flag lets us scope bazelrc settings to specific scenarios. @laszlocsomor do you think we should have a feature request so that --watchfs could be disabled on a single platform? OR maybe we should just disable the feature on windows generally?
